1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:09,301
The brush clears a bronze lamp, with a bowl for oil. Chola temples were lit by lamps like this, given by villagers and kings.

2
00:00:09,301 --> 00:00:14,284
The same temples hold, on their walls, the rules for electing the village council.

3
00:00:14,284 --> 00:00:18,260
How did a village choose its leaders a thousand years ago?

4
00:00:35,050 --> 00:00:42,730
How do we know? The Uttaramerur inscriptions, from the time of Parantaka the First, record the rules of the village council.

5
00:00:42,730 --> 00:00:49,392
Archaeologists dug up Chola villages. Few places show village rule so clearly.

6
00:01:04,683 --> 00:01:11,785
Chola villages ran their own affairs. The village assembly was called the ur, or the sabha in Brahmin villages.

7
00:01:11,785 --> 00:01:17,202
The Uttaramerur inscriptions record the rules for the sabha, about 920 CE.

8
00:01:17,202 --> 00:01:22,050
Each village was divided into thirty wards, and each ward chose one member.

9
00:01:22,050 --> 00:01:27,675
Candidates had to own land, have a home, be of a certain age, and know the Vedas.

10
00:01:27,675 --> 00:01:32,458
They could not have held office in the last three years, or have been guilty of crime.

11
00:01:32,458 --> 00:01:37,528
Names were written on palm leaves, put into a pot, and a child drew one out.

12
00:01:37,528 --> 00:01:41,325
This was called the kudavolai system, or election by lot.

13
00:01:41,325 --> 00:01:49,331
The elected members formed committees, called variyams, for tanks, gardens and justice. The temple was the hub of the village.

14
00:01:49,331 --> 00:01:58,225
It owned land, employed many, lent money, and ran schools. The state took a land tax and measured fields carefully.

15
00:02:13,517 --> 00:02:17,957
Scholars disagree. How centralised was the Chola state?

16
00:02:17,957 --> 00:02:23,309
One view sees a strong central kingdom, with officers, land surveys and a large army.

17
00:02:23,309 --> 00:02:32,246
Another view sees a segmentary state, where local assemblies and temples held much of the real power, and the king's rule was mostly ritual authority.

18
00:02:32,246 --> 00:02:35,752
Both views use the same inscriptions.

19
00:02:51,050 --> 00:03:01,006
Carve this tip into memory. Thirty wards, pot and palm leaf. a child draws the lot. Thirty wards, a pot, and a child.

20
00:03:01,006 --> 00:03:04,433
That is how a Chola village chose its council.

21
00:03:19,750 --> 00:03:31,924
Dig Quiz. Pause and name it. Number one. Which inscriptions describe the village council elections?

22
00:03:31,924 --> 00:03:47,926
The answer: the Uttaramerur inscriptions. Number two. What was election by lot called? The answer: kudavolai. Number three.

23
00:03:47,926 --> 00:03:59,092
What were the village committees called? The answer: variyams. Now one line for Mains.

24
00:03:59,092 --> 00:04:03,122
Discuss the working of local self-government under the Cholas.

25
00:04:22,417 --> 00:04:30,133
The bronze lamp goes into its case. Chola temples were lit by lamps like this. Three facts to take away.

26
00:04:30,133 --> 00:04:38,219
A lamp given to a Chola temple. Uttaramerur: elections by lot. Temples as centres of village life.

27
00:04:38,219 --> 00:04:42,500
Next gallery: Three Powers, One Prize.

